// ADD YOUR CODE.
//
// This file is the public face of the system: the one thing code outside the
// library should have to reach for. In your chosen language, that means the
// public class/interface declaration lives here, and everything it is built
// from lives in intern/ (see the assignment handout, section 6, for how each
// language expresses that boundary).
//
// The shape of what you declare here:
//
//   inputs :  a[0..3] : BIT, b[0..3] : BIT, cin : BIT
//   outputs:  sum[0..3] : BIT, cout : BIT
//
//   every setter recomputes sum and cout before returning - that is the
//   AbstractDevice contract (handout, section 5)
//
// Four full-adders chained in ripple-carry order: the carry-out of bit i
// feeds the carry-in of bit i+1, and the external cin feeds bit 0.
